          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਉਸਾਰਨਾ — usārnā — \"to put up a building; to build\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੇਰਾ ਪਿਤਾ ਪਿੰਡ ਵਿੱਚ ਘਰ ਉਸਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ। merā pitā piṇḍ vich ghar usārdā hai. My father builds houses in the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਇੱਕ ਕਮਰਾ ਉਸਾਰਿਆ, maiṁ ikk kamrā usāriā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਉਸਾਰਨਾ (usārnā) is the transitive partner of ussarṇā, \"to rise (of a building)\", which goes back to Sanskrit útsarati, \"hastens away\", with a sense \"rises\" that CDIAL infers; CDIAL lists Punjabi ussarṇā under it (CDIAL 1874), but not the transitive form itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
